'''Tama''' is an extinct indigenous [[Tucanoan languages|Tucanoan language]] of [[Colombia]].<ref name="ethnologue">[http://www.ethnologue.com/show_language.asp?code=ten Ethnologue report for language code:ten]</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last=Mora Cortes |first=Luis Emilio |date=1992 |title=La Dominancia Nasal en la Variedad Tama |url=https://revistas.unal.edu.co/index.php/formayfuncion/article/download/16940/17799 |journal=Forma y Función |volume=6 |pages=91–102}}</ref> It was spoken in the regions of [[Vicente (Colombia)|Vicente]], [[Orteguaza River]] and [[Caquetá Department|Caquetá Region]].

